// soot — funideas §8, the smallest true version of it: a fire that leaves a
// stain where it lands, and nobody wrote a "make this floor sooty" system.
//
// `row.stuck` is 1 for a landed row and 0 for one still in the air, so the
// amount IS the condition — an airborne row asks for nothing and nothing is
// what it leaves. The mark is as wide as the ember, decays on the channel's
// own clock, and accumulates where the embers keep landing.
//
// The spray's `casts` could not do this. A cast is one aggregate at the
// centre of the cloud, restated every tick; this is many marks, where the
// rows actually were, that outlive the rows that made them.

spawn
gravity plane.drift.@self.k.gravity
collide | stick
perish

// A landed ember is a small stain; the seed gives them different widths.
row.seed | mul 0.05 | add 0.05 | write row.size
row.stuck | mul plane.drift.@self.k.stain | deposit $soot
